GMXtransplant roadmap and working log
=====================================

Read this first when continuing on another computer. The newest entry is at
the bottom of the log section.

Setting up a new computer
-------------------------
  git clone <repo> && cd GMXtransplant
  ~/miniforge3/bin/python3 -m pip install .        # install into the base conda env
  python3 tools/run_tests.py --fast                # about 2 min; full suite without --fast (~7 min)
  QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -m unittest tests.test_gui

Working rules
-------------
- No Claude attribution in commits or PRs (no Co-Authored-By, no "Generated with").
- No CI: never add GitHub Actions or any test runs on GitHub. All testing is local.
- Install into the base conda env (command above), not a separate env.
- Keep the laptop cool: long or multi-threaded GROMACS runs go to Dardel through
  Slurm (account naiss2025-3-21, modules PDC/26.03 gromacs/2026.1-cpeGNU-26.03,
  `srun gmx_mpi`), never on the login node. `gmxtransplant slurm-script <folder>
  --profile dardel --account naiss2025-3-21` writes submit.sh.
- GUI: keep the original titles and labels. Main modes and examples stay visible;
  newer modes and extra examples go under "More modes" / "More examples".
- Files named *.local.md are local notes and are never committed.

Modes (gmxtransplant --mode ...)
--------------------------------
  charmprot, protein, lig, chl, addbinder     original pipelines
  membrane                                        replace the membrane: bundled POPC, or any bilayer via reference_gro
  salt, protonate, mutate, hmr,               system-edit modes (src/mode_registry.py, src/system_edit.py);
  resize, flood, oligomer                     guide docs/guides/EDIT_MODES.md, examples/<mode>/
  check-gromacs, slurm-script                 subcommands

Open items / roadmap
--------------------
1. membrane: run the full 1.875 ns equilibration on Dardel with the merged engine
   (2 A removal distances). Only grompp + minimization + 5 ps NVT have been
   run on it so far (job 26435453); the full run (job 26430209) used the old
   engine with 3 A distances.
2. PDBFixer pipelines (planned, not implemented): docs/guides/PDBFIXER_ROADMAP.md
   - mutate side chains from PDBFixer, protonation states from pH, a prepare
     step for incoming structures, loops and termini, comparison benchmark.
3. addbinder: verify a Gs heterotrimer on the D1R intracellular side
   (docs/guides/ADDBINDER_ROADMAP.md for the addbinder roadmap).
4. Host artifact: minimizations of the D1R example host stop at 5000 steps on
   POPE 807 C210 (atom 62006); this comes from the host build, not our modes.
5. Housekeeping: the local branch pre-strip-backup can be deleted once confirmed.

